{'symbol': 'ABBV', 'date': '2019-11-06 22:30:00', 'title': 'Abbvie Announces Launch of Private Offering of Senior Unsecured Notes', 'text': 'AbbVie Inc. announced that it has launched a private offering (the "Offering") of senior unsecured notes (the "Notes"). The Offering is being conducted in connection with AbbVie\'s previously announced acquisition (the "Acquisition") of Allergan plc ("Allergan"). AbbVie expects to use the net proceeds from the Offering to fund a portion of the aggregate cash consideration due to Allergan shareholders in connection with the Acquisition and to pay related fees and expenses, with any remaining net proceeds being used for general corporate purposes. Consummation of the Offering is subject to market and other conditions. The Notes have not been registered under the Securities Act of 1933, as amended (the "Securities Act"), any state securities laws or the securities laws of any other jurisdiction, and may not be offered or sold in the United States, or for the benefit of U.S. persons, except pursuant to an applicable exemption from, or in a transaction not subject to, the registration requirements of the Securities Act and applicable state securities or blue sky laws. Accordingly, the Notes are being offered in the United States only to persons reasonably believed to be "qualified institutional buyers," as that term is defined under Rule 144A of the Securities Act, or outside the United States to non-"U.S. persons" in accordance with Regulation S under the Securities Act. A confidential offering memorandum for the Offering of the Notes, dated as of it, is being made available to such eligible persons. The Offering is being conducted in accordance with the terms and subject to the conditions set forth in such confidential offering memorandum.'}
{'symbol': 'AES', 'date': '2019-11-06 11:30:00', 'title': 'AES Corp Reports Q3 Adjusted Earnings Per Share Of $0.48', 'text': 'AES DELIVERS STRONG THIRD QUARTER RESULTS AND ACCELERATES STRATEGIC PLANS.REAFFIRMS FY 2019 ADJUSTED EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $1.30 TO $1.38.Q3 ADJUSTED NON-GAAP EARNINGS PER SHARE $0.48.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE $0.32 FROM CONTINUING OPERATIONS.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE ESTIMATE $0.41 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE $0.32.REAFFIRMING 2019 GUIDANCE AND 7% TO 9% AVERAGE ANNUAL GROWTH TARGET FOR ADJUSTED EPS AND PARENT FREE CASH FLOW THROUGH 2022.FY2019 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $1.34, REVENUE VIEW $10.68 BILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.QTRLY TOTAL REVENUE $2,625 MILLION VERSUS $2,837 MILLION.Q3 REVENUE VIEW $2.96 BILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.'}
{'symbol': 'AES', 'date': '2019-11-06 22:30:00', 'title': 'the Aes Corporation Reports Earnings Results for the Third Quarter Ended September 30, 2019', 'text': 'The AES Corporation announced earnings results for the third quarter ended September 30, 2019. For the third quarter, the company announced total revenue was USD 2,625 million compared to USD 2,837 million a year ago. Net income was USD 210 million compared to USD 101 million a year ago. Basic earnings per share was USD 0.32 compared to USD 0.15 a year ago. For the nine months, total revenue was USD 7,758 million compared to USD 8,114 million a year ago. Net income was USD 381 million compared to USD 1,075 million a year ago. Basic earnings per share from continuing operations was USD 0.57 compared to USD 1.33 a year ago. Basic earnings per share was USD 0.57 compared to USD 1.62 a year ago.'}
